WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.526
Moving session and application state out of a web
process makes that process easier to duplicate The

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:12.138
shared database now carries durable data and
coordinates changes made by those copies.

00:00:12.138 --> 00:00:12.334
No.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:17.162
All copies may still wait on the same overloaded
database or storage path.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.282
A relational schema describes tables, columns and
relationships A staff row can refer to one

00:00:23.282 --> 00:00:26.918
department, and a department can refer to one
building.

00:00:26.918 --> 00:00:33.132
With the shown normalized schema, one department row
changes; staff references retain the same

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.587
department identifier.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:40.782
An index stores an additional access path to rows
Without a suitable access path, a query may scan

00:00:40.782 --> 00:00:42.863
many rows to find a small result.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:43.053
No.

00:00:43.053 --> 00:00:49.108
It can increase write maintenance and storage cost
without helping the queries that dominate the

00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:49.676
workload.
